  "interpretation_guide": "Teacher-forced on the reference's saved plan; not free-generation accuracy. If reference attention substantially improves predictions while transferred values are retained, a small receiver-side attention adjustment or query adapter is worth investigating. If it gives little improvement, investigate selective reconstruction of result states; that would not prove every attention adjustment must fail. If it improves distribution matching but not label decisions, report the distinction and examine where generation diverges before training anything. A promising result needs a follow-up where reference and intervention share the same actual generated history. This is an oracle diagnostic, not a method."
